Review follow-ups: noteUse re-holds immediately (no 15 s gap before a released
backend's idle grace could end), the post-resume rebuild filter lives in
SshKeepaliveHolds.rebuildIfHeld with its own log line and tests (dead unheld
scope retired, not redialled; bare/local/non-SSH/default/prewarm/recent
redialled), a release cancels a pending reconnect (mutation-checked), and the
warm-set test cleans its temp dir.
---
 apps/desktop/electron/main.ts                 |  4 +-
 .../electron/ssh-keepalive-hold.test.ts       | 65 ++++++++++++++++++-
 apps/desktop/electron/ssh-keepalive-hold.ts   | 17 +++++
 3 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts b/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts
index 47530c5e921..51ecac2e103 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts
+++ b/apps/desktop/electron/main.ts
@@ -14266,9 +14266,7 @@ function revalidateSuspectPoolAfterResume() {
       entries: backendPool.entries(),
       log: rememberLog,
       probe: (connection, path, options) => fetchJsonForBackend(connection, path, options),
-      // A dead scope outside the warm/in-use set is only retired: rebuilding it would re-pin it.
-      rebuild: async poolKey =>
-        remoteWarmSet.holds.shouldHold(poolKey) ? redialPoolBackendAfterResume(poolKey) : undefined,
+      rebuild: poolKey => remoteWarmSet.holds.rebuildIfHeld(poolKey, redialPoolBackendAfterResume),
       retire: async poolKey => {
         await stopPoolBackend(poolKey, 'resume')
         // The pool key doubles as the SSH scope for registry SSH backends and
diff --git a/apps/desktop/electron/ssh-keepalive-hold.test.ts b/apps/desktop/electron/ssh-keepalive-hold.test.ts
index ac539bda221..8fe34b95ddc 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/electron/ssh-keepalive-hold.test.ts
